  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 123 AM CDT Wed Aug 12 2026\n\nMid-level high pressure will dominate the period leading to warm and \nmostly rain free conditions outside of isolated seabreeze convection \neach day. As we encroaching on the end of the week, we will see an \ninverted trough tracking along the southern periphery of the ridge. \nThis will lead to a increase in moisture region, surging PWATs \naround 2.0 inches (75th percentile of climatology). Expect this to \nbe accompanied with some associated vorticity which will allow for \nsome at least low rain chances (~20%) during the day Friday. Will \ncontinue to monitor the need for some short- fused heat related \nproducts. We could see heat indices up to 115 at times with dew \npoints around the mid to upper 70s present through the next week. \nThis translates to Moderate to Extreme heat stress conditions. We \nstrongly encourage the practice of heat safety in these conditions. \nTake frequent breaks and remember to stay hydrated, check those \nbackseats, and avoid long exposure in these temperatures. For more \ninformation be sure to check out weather.gov/heatsafety.",
